infinite-patch 1
# Spectrum Slide: one voice turns into another by moving its partials, not by cross-fading.
# band Sound
node 1 Notes Random Note Generator
  id notes
  pos 0 600
  i scale natural minor
  i root A
  i rangeLow 45
  i rangeHigh 64
  f rateBeats 1
end
node 2 Synths Wavetable
  id voice
  pos 480 600
  i a.table Vocal
  f volume 0.5
end
node 3 Synths Analog
  id saw
  pos 480 1970
  i wave1 saw
  f cutoff 6000
  f volume 0.5
end
node 4 AudioEffects Spectrum Slide
  id slide
  pos 1640 600
end
node 5 Modulators LFO
  id sweep
  pos 0 3130
  f rateBeats 16
end
node 6 Utility Audio Out
  id speakers
  pos 2260 600
end
node 7 Compositing Comment
  pos -520 0
  s text Spectrum Slide morphs "audio" into "to" by optimal transport of their spectra: at slide 0.5 a partial at 440 Hz in one and 880 Hz in the other sounds at 660 Hz, not as two half-level peaks. The LFO sweeps slide 0..1 over four bars.
  f width 360
  f height 120
end
node 8 Source Shape
  id picture
  pos 0 0
  i shapeType Blob
end
node 9 Utility Output
  id out
  pos 460 0
end
note voice 0 notes
note saw 0 notes
aud slide 0 voice
aud slide 1 saw
aud speakers 0 slide
mod slide slide sweep 0 0 1 0.5
cable out 0 picture
